---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { APP_STORE_URL, PLAY_STORE_URL, pathFor } from '../../config/site';
---
<SiteLayout title="Help with gentle games and family photos" description="Version-specific Golden Moments help for picture matching, selected family photos, offline activities, and safe troubleshooting.">
  <section class="interior-hero"><div class="reading-column">
    <p class="eyebrow">A simple guide</p><h1>Help with Golden Moments</h1>
    <p class="interior-lede">Start small, follow the person's interests, and stop whenever you like.</p>
  </div></section>
  <div class="reading-column prose-page">
    <aside class="planned-note"><strong>Check your version first</strong><span>The steps below describe the upcoming 1.3.0 update. Store review and release are pending. Earlier versions may have different screens and do not include personal-photo activities. Check the version available on the <a href={APP_STORE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">App Store</a> or <a href={PLAY_STORE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play</a>.</span></aside>
    <h2>Start a gentle game</h2>
    <p>In version 1.3.0, choose <strong>Start a gentle game</strong>. The first board has four large tiles with pictures visible. Tap two matching pictures. There is no timer, score, or penalty. Choose <strong>Done for now</strong> whenever you want to leave.</p>
    <h2>Adjust the pictures</h2>
    <p>Open <strong>Comfort settings</strong> in the gentle game to change the tile count or whether pictures stay visible. Available choices depend on the number of pictures. Your gentle-play choices are saved on this device. You can return to a smaller board at any time.</p>
    <h2>Choose family photos</h2>
    <p>In version 1.3.0, open <strong>Your family photos</strong>, then <strong>Choose photos</strong>. Select only pictures you have permission to use and that the person is comfortable seeing. The app keeps smaller copies of up to 24 selected photos in one local collection. It does not scan the rest of your library or change your originals.</p>
    <p>Use at least two different pictures for matching, or choose <strong>Look at photos together</strong> with just one picture. Optional conversation prompts have no correct answer. Simply looking together is enough.</p>
    <h2>Use the app offline</h2>
    <p>Version 1.3.0 includes all eight picture packs, so they need no separate image downloads. Saved photo copies work offline after import. If an original is stored only in iCloud or another cloud photo service, your device may need internet to retrieve it before import.</p>
    <h2>Remove a copy safely</h2>
    <p>Use the photo collection's remove controls and review the confirmation before continuing. Removal affects the app's copies, not the originals in your photo library. There is no family-photo sync service or in-app transfer to another device. Device backups may include app data, depending on your settings.</p>
    <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
    <p>If selecting photos is cancelled, try again when ready. If an import fails, keep the originals and try a smaller selection. If a screen is stuck, close and reopen the app. Do not delete the app or clear its storage as a first troubleshooting step: doing so can remove saved copies and preferences.</p>
    <p>If pictures or saved data appear missing, stop making changes and <a href={pathFor('/support/')}>contact support</a>. Include your device, OS, app version, and what happened. Please do not send private photos, passwords, or medical details.</p>
    <h2>Comfort comes first</h2>
    <p>Offer choices rather than asking someone to remember a name or finish a board. Change the picture or stop if it feels uncomfortable. Golden Moments offers recreation and conversation; it does not diagnose, measure, treat, or prevent dementia or Alzheimer's disease.</p>
    <p><a href={pathFor('/app-privacy/')}>App privacy</a> · <a href={pathFor('/privacy-choices/')}>Deletion choices</a> · <a href={pathFor('/terms/')}>Terms and license</a> · <a href={pathFor('/support/')}>Contact support</a></p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
